# Line endings in the working tree are LF on every platform.
#
# This repository's tests compare command output against committed
# expected artifacts byte for byte (cli/testdata/cases/**/expected/), and
# .github/workflows/cli.yml runs them on windows-latest, where Git's
# default `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise rewrite both the fixture
# corpora and the expected artifacts on checkout. Pinning the working
# tree to LF is what lets one set of expected bytes be the answer on all
# three platforms.
#
# It does not weaken the CRLF guarantee AC-SPEC-009.7 makes — it is what
# makes that guarantee testable. The CRLF checkout the criterion names is
# reproduced synthetically, on every platform, by
# cli/cmd/portability_test.go, which replays every case from a working
# tree it has rewritten to CRLF itself.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
